/*=============================================================================
🧠 SYSTEMVERILOG — EVENTS (PROCESS SYNCHRONIZATION)
=============================================================================

📘 Concept:
- Events are used for **synchronization between processes**.
- No data is transferred — only a signal or trigger.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
🔹 Declaration:
   event start_e;

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
🔹 Operations:
   -> start_e;     // trigger (raise event)
   @(start_e);     // wait for event to occur
   wait_order(e1, e2); // wait for sequence of events

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
🔹 Example Summary:
   • Driver waits for event (@start_e)
   • Generator triggers event after 20ns (-> start_e)
   • Driver resumes and starts work

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
🔹 Example Output:
   Driver waiting for generator...
   Generator ready, triggering event!
   Driver started at 20

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
🔹 Important Notes:
✅ If event triggered before process waits, signal is lost.
✅ Multiple waiters → all wake up when event triggered.
✅ Does not store history (stateless synchronization).

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
🔹 Real DV Applications:
✅ Phase coordination (reset_done, test_start)
✅ Start/stop control between parallel threads
✅ Inter-component signaling in testbench
✅ Basic handshake modeling between Generator/Driver

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
🔹 Comparison Summary:
   Event      → Synchronization signal
   Mailbox    → Data communication
   Semaphore  → Resource control

💡 Events are the foundation of process synchronization in testbenches.
=============================================================================
END OF NOTES
=============================================================================*/
